{
    "article_summary": "The article describes a photoredox-enabled remote radical group migration using diazoalkanes as radical precursors to synthesize 1,7-dicarbonyl compounds. Using Ru(bpy)3Cl2 as a photocatalyst under blue LED irradiation, the method facilitates the addition of alkyl radicals to unactivated olefins followed by the migration of various heteroaryl groups (benzothiazole, pyridine, etc.) or nitrile groups, resulting in the formation of two C-C bonds and one C-O bond in a single process.",
